DEBUG-ONLY guest-driver patch (NOT for production — production must run the
stock open driver). Confirms the Mode-2 cuCtxCreate SIGSEGV root cause and
unblocks progress to the next blocker.

Root cause (see memory mode2_cuctxcreate_crash_root_cause): the GR-object
(AMPERE_COMPUTE_B 0xc7c0) RM_ALLOC copies a 16-byte NV_GR_ALLOCATION_PARAMETERS
back into libcuda's 8-byte pAllocParms stack slot, clobbering a saved rbp ->
SIGSEGV. The real GSP makes the stock driver copy 0 bytes (host proves it); our
fake GSP makes it copy 16. This patch makes the guest driver null pAllocParms for
GR-object allocs so the OPTIONAL param becomes a no-copy (matches host).

Apply to nvidia/nv.c, in nvidia_ioctl(), right after the NV_COPY_FROM_USER block:

    if (arg_cmd == 0x2b /* NV_ESC_RM_ALLOC */ && arg_copy != NULL &&
        (arg_size == 48 /*NVOS64*/ || arg_size == 40 /*NVOS21*/)) {
        NvU32 _hc = *(NvU32 *)((char *)arg_copy + 12);   /* hClass */
        NvU32 _lb = _hc & 0xff, _fam = (_hc >> 8) & 0xff;
        if (_fam >= 0xb0 && (_lb == 0xc0 || _lb == 0x97)) {  /* GR compute/3D */
            *(NvU64 *)((char *)arg_copy + 16) = 0;           /* NULL pAllocParms */
            printk(KERN_INFO "NVKVMDBG null pAllocParms GR class 0x%x\n", _hc);
        }
    }

RESULT (2026-06-04, fresh boot): cuCtxCreate SIGSEGV -> gone; now returns
CUDA error 999 (next blocker). Build: mount 9p ogkm, copy source to tmpfs,
make modules SYSSRC=/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build. Staged in guest at
~/nvmods-dbg/nvidia.ko.

